        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Concepts: opéra comique\n- Places: Paris theatre\n- Products: Carmen, Aida\n- People: Georges Bizet, Henri Meilhac, Ludovic Halévy, Prosper Mérimée, Giuseppe Verdi, Nell Rankin\n- Roles: Amneris\n\nFacts:\n- Opéra comique is associated with a Paris theatre of the same name.\n- Opéra comique is not always comic or light in nature.\n- Carmen is often considered the most famous opéra comique, and Carmen is a tragedy.\n- Carmen is an opera in four acts by French composer Georges Bizet.\n- The libretto for Carmen was written by Henri Meilhac and Ludovic Halévy.\n- Carmen is based on a novella of the same title by Prosper Mérimée.\n- Nell Rankin was particularly admired for her portrayals of Amneris in Giuseppe Verdi's Aida and the title role in Georges Bizet's Carmen.",
